  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REPP - Renewable Energy Performance Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Renewable Energy Performance Platform (REPP) is a private finance investment vehicle which mobilises private sector development activity and investment into small- to medium-scale renewable energy projects across sub-Saharan Africa. This is through providing technical assistance, development capital and &#x2018;viability gap&#x2019; financing, giving communities access to clean energy supplies and avoiding greenhouse gas emissions.

REPP was initially set up by the Department for Business, Energy &amp; Industrial Strategy (BEIS) in 2015 but was transferred to the FCDO in 2022. REPP consequently has a separate DevTracker account under BEIS which can be found here - https://devtracker.fcdo.gov.uk/programme/GB-GOV-13-ICF-0013-REPP/summary.</narrative>
  </description>
